# Process-lifetime System-backed route array retained by an mmap registry heap.
# See fuzz/README.md for lifecycle, evidence, and an unsuppressed audit command.
# Wildcards on both ends: the CI symbolizer (llvm-symbolizer with debug info)
# prints the allocation frame's function name as the bare, namespace-free
# `ensure_capacity` (observed in scheduled run 38260710015, job 114850160710,
# frame #5), so a namespace-qualified pattern like
# `route_slots::RouteSlots*::ensure_capacity` never matched and the leak was
# still reported. `*ensure_capacity*` matches that bare name and any
# namespace-qualified rendering of the same site; the method name is unique to
# this call site in the tree (verified by grep), so this stays a narrow,
# site-specific suppression and does not hide unrelated leaks.
leak:*ensure_capacity*
